+--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
+SATELLITE 004: satellite.file
+--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
+
+satellite.file is the words that reach a file by its path: two that make or
+open one and answer a handle, and two that answer a question about a path. The
+handle is a satellite.variable.file, a text file held as a list of lines --
+satellite.help(satellite.variable.file) says what you can do with one.
+
+    satellite.file.new(path)            makes a text file that is not there,
+                                        and answers it open and empty
+    satellite.file.new(path, "text")    the same, with the kind named
+    satellite.file.open(path)           opens a text file that is there
+    satellite.file.open(path, "text")   the same, with the kind named
+    satellite.file.exists(path)         true when a file is at the path; a
+                                        directory answers false
+    satellite.file.clear(path)          empties a file that is there, by name,
+                                        and leaves it there; true when it did
+
+new never clobbers: when anything is already at the path -- a file, a folder, a
+link -- nothing is made, what is there is untouched, and the handle is not ok.
+open never creates: a path with no file at it gives a handle that is not ok
+and makes nothing, so a misspelt path cannot quietly become an empty file.
+A folder, a FIFO or a device given as the file is not a file, and the handle
+says so.
+
+A file that would not open is a value, not an error. new and open always answer
+a handle and never stop the program: a file that could not be made or opened is
+a handle whose ok is false and whose error says why, in words -- what is at the
+path, what is missing, or what the system said. The program goes on, so it can
+ask f.ok and choose. What does stop a program is asking such a handle about its
+lines -- f.size, f[1], f.search(x) -- because the only answers it could give
+would be made up (S503, exit 45): ask ok first.
+
+The kinds are "text" and "binary", and new and open take "text" when nothing is
+said. A text file is UTF-8 on the disk and satellite strings in the program; a
+file whose bytes are not UTF-8 opens as a handle that is not ok, and error
+names the line and the byte. The lines end as the file had them, so a file
+written with \r\n keeps \r\n, and a byte-order mark at the top is kept and is
+no part of line 1. A file whose lines end in \r alone is refused by name.
+"binary" is not built yet: satellite.file.new("b.bin", "binary") answers a
+handle that is not ok, and its error says binary files are not built yet.
+
+Where a path points. A path with no leading / is relative to the folder of the
+.satl file the line is written in -- not to where satl was started from, and
+not to the folder a satellite.directory.change moved to -- so a program finds
+its own files wherever it is run from. A path with a leading / is looked for
+under the program's own folder first, and then at the root of the filesystem:
+"/story/one.se" reaches the program's own story/ folder when there is one. For
+new, which makes something, it is the folder that must already be there. At
+the prompt there is no program file, so a path is the working directory's. A
+path holding a NUL is refused. f.path answers the whole path, from /, that the
+handle opened -- not the path as it was written -- and the handle keeps that,
+so a change of directory after the open cannot send a save to another file.
+
+A handle made by new or open stays open until it is closed, or until the
+capsule or block that named it ends, when it is saved and closed for you.
+
+Not built yet: a read-only open, satellite.file.open(path, "text", "read"),
+where every changing word would answer false and the file is never rewritten.
+Today the third argument is refused before anything runs (S110).
+
+example:
+
+satellite.include(satellite)
+
+satellite.capsule satellite.main()
+{
+    satellite.console.display(satellite.file.exists("notes.se")) // false
+    satellite.variable.file notes = satellite.file.new("notes.se")
+    satellite.console.display(notes.ok) // true
+    notes.append("first note")
+    satellite.console.display(satellite.file.exists("notes.se")) // true
+    satellite.variable.file twice = satellite.file.new("notes.se")
+    satellite.console.display(twice.ok) // false -- new never clobbers
+    satellite.console.display(twice.error) // something is already at ...notes.se, and new never replaces it: nothing was made (open opens it)
+    satellite.variable.file missing = satellite.file.open("no_such.se")
+    satellite.console.display(missing.ok) // false -- open never creates
+    satellite.console.display(satellite.file.exists("no_such.se")) // false
+    satellite.variable.file wrong = satellite.file.new("b.bin", "binary")
+    satellite.console.display(wrong.ok) // false
+    satellite.console.display(wrong.error) // binary files are not built yet (SATELLITE_FILE_OPERATIONS FO-8)
+    satellite.console.display(notes.close()) // true
+    satellite.console.display(satellite.file.clear("notes.se")) // true
+    satellite.console.display(satellite.file.clear("no_such.se")) // false
+    satellite.variable.file again = satellite.file.open("notes.se")
+    satellite.console.display(again.size) // 0
+    satellite.console.display(again.path) // the whole path from /, ending in /notes.se
+    satellite.return(satellite)
+}
+
+refused when it runs -- a question put to a handle that is not ok (S503):
+
+satellite.include(satellite)
+
+satellite.capsule satellite.main()
+{
+    satellite.variable.file missing = satellite.file.open("no_such.se")
+    satellite.console.display(missing.ok) // false, and the program goes on
+    satellite.console.display(missing.size) // stops here: S503, exit 45
+    satellite.return(satellite)
+}
